Polish geographic locality annotations

Contains data from Główny Urząd Geodezji i Kartografii (GUGiK),
Państwowy Rejestr Granic (PRG), supplied through the sixteen Polish provincial
OpenAddresses datasets in the installer's pinned Overture address release.
https://www.geoportal.gov.pl/pl/dane/panstwowy-rejestr-granic-prg/
https://www.geoportal.gov.pl/en/about-geoportal/terms-and-conditions/

The supplied rows identify LicenseRef-Public-Domain-PL-Geodesy-Law. The official
Geoportal terms permit reuse and publication with attribution (Article 3).
This notice retains that attribution; it does not assert CC BY or worldwide
public-domain status. Existing Overture/OpenAddresses attribution also applies.

The source definitions at OpenAddresses commit
76ac33513648f1c050f2d09c2bfdc0376f2514f6 map CITY to PRG's miejscowosc,
ID to lokalnyId, and NUMBER to numerPorzadkowy, separately from kodPocztowy.
https://github.com/openaddresses/openaddresses/tree/76ac33513648f1c050f2d09c2bfdc0376f2514f6/sources/pl
The processed datasets/versions/update times used are in poland-source.json.
The September/October 2026 Overture releases encode these geographic levels as
[powiat, province, miejscowosc] / [province, gmina, miejscowosc], respectively.
Exactly one of the first two levels must identify the dataset's province;
missing or contradictory province evidence is rejected in either layout.

Modified: geographic locality names are matched to uniquely named indexed
localities below the inherited parent, in the source province. Membership is
attached only to a final selected house with the identical packed source point
and complete number. Conflicting names, ambiguous descendants, unsupported
provenance, changed/averaged points and incompatible regions are omitted.
No SIMC/TERYT crosswalk, postal-to-geographic equivalence or nearest-place
membership is inferred. Evaluation samples are not an index input.
